IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc24-appeal-procedure`

-- ccc24-tests-appeal-procedure.l4 -- tests for ccc24-appeal-procedure.l4 (Criminal Code ss 678 to 689).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section, row by row, before the run.
-- Results: T = JUST TRUE, F = JUST FALSE, N = NOTHING.  Fixtures: short names for the long constructors (prefix `ccc24 fixture`).

`ccc24 fixture 679a` MEANS `s 679(1)(a) an appeal to the court of appeal against conviction`
`ccc24 fixture 679b` MEANS `s 679(1)(b) an appeal to the court of appeal against sentence only`
`ccc24 fixture 679c` MEANS `s 679(1)(c) an appeal or an application for leave to appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada`
`ccc24 fixture 679x` MEANS `s 679(1) an appeal of another kind`

§ `Section 678`

-- (1): the period is the rules'; a notice inside it is given as required; one outside it is not covered (678(2) lets the court extend "at any time").
#ASSERT `s 678(1) the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal was given in the manner and within the period directed by rules of court` TRUE 5 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 678(1) the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal was given in the manner and within the period directed by rules of court` TRUE 10 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day is "within"
#ASSERT `s 678(1) the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal was given in the manner and within the period directed by rules of court` TRUE 11 10 EQUALS NOTHING   -- a day late: not covered (fork F678), not FALSE
#ASSERT `s 678(1) the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal was given in the manner and within the period directed by rules of court` FALSE 5 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 678(2) the court of appeal or a judge may extend the time for giving notice of appeal or of an application for leave to appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 678(2) the court of appeal or a judge may extend the time for giving notice of appeal or of an application for leave to appeal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 678.1 service of the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal may be effected substitutionally` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 678.1 service of the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal may be effected substitutionally` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where a respondent cannot be found": a where-gate

§ `Section 679`

#ASSERT `s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal` `ccc24 fixture 679a` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) notice given
#ASSERT `s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal` `ccc24 fixture 679a` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a) no notice: not covered
#ASSERT `s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal` `ccc24 fixture 679b` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) leave granted
#ASSERT `s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal` `ccc24 fixture 679b` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b) no leave
#ASSERT `s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal` `ccc24 fixture 679c` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c) filed and served
#ASSERT `s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal` `ccc24 fixture 679c` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal` `ccc24 fixture 679x` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another kind of appeal
#ASSERT `s 679(2) the appellant must give written notice of the application for release to the prosecutor or to another person a judge of the court of appeal directs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(2) the appellant must give written notice of the application for release to the prosecutor or to another person a judge of the court of appeal directs` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where an appellant applies"
#ASSERT `s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada` `ccc24 fixture 679a` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada` `ccc24 fixture 679c` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada` `ccc24 fixture 679a` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- frivolous: not established
#ASSERT `s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada` `ccc24 fixture 679a` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no surrender
#ASSERT `s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada` `ccc24 fixture 679a` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- detention necessary in the public interest
#ASSERT `s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada` `ccc24 fixture 679b` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a sentence-only appeal is (4)'s
#ASSERT `s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada` `ccc24 fixture 679x` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 679(4) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against sentence only` `ccc24 fixture 679b` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(4) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against sentence only` `ccc24 fixture 679b` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no sufficient merit
#ASSERT `s 679(4) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against sentence only` `ccc24 fixture 679b` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 679(4) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against sentence only` `ccc24 fixture 679b` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 679(4) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against sentence only` `ccc24 fixture 679a` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a conviction appeal is (3)'s
#ASSERT `s 679(5) the judge must make a release order referred to in section 515 that includes a condition that the accused surrender themselves into custody` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(5) the judge must make a release order referred to in section 515 that includes a condition that the accused surrender themselves into custody` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "If the judge ... does not refuse"
#ASSERT `s 679(5.1) the person having custody of the appellant must immediately release the appellant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(5.1) the person having custody of the appellant must immediately release the appellant` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if the appellant complies"
-- 679(5.1) as a regulative rule: release on day 0 is FULFILLED; a lapse of one day with no release is a BREACH.  Compared across both stable builds.
#TRACE `s 679(5.1) the immediate release rule` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `s 679(5.1) release the appellant` AT 0

#TRACE `s 679(5.1) the immediate release rule` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1)

#ASSERT `s 679(6) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the proceedings under section 679` 495.1 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(6) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the proceedings under section 679` 512.3 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(6) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the proceedings under section 679` 524 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(6) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the proceedings under section 679` 515 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a list that does not say "only"
#ASSERT `s 679(6) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the proceedings under section 679` 524 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 679(7) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person pending the hearing and determination of the reference as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(7) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person pending the hearing and determination of the reference as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 679(7.1) section 515 or 522 applies to the release or detention of the person pending the new trial or new hearing as though the person were charged with the offence for the first time, the powers being exercised by a judge of the court of appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(7.1) section 515 or 522 applies to the release or detention of the person pending the new trial or new hearing as though the person were charged with the offence for the first time, the powers being exercised by a judge of the court of appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 679(8) section 679 applies to the application for leave to appeal or the appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada in summary conviction proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(8) section 679 applies to the application for leave to appeal or the appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada in summary conviction proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 679(10) a judge may give the directions the judge thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal, the new trial, the new hearing or the hearing of the reference` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- CoA judge, on the appellant's application, no order under (5)
#ASSERT `s 679(10) a judge may give the directions the judge thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal, the new trial, the new hearing or the hearing of the reference` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- cancels an earlier order
#ASSERT `s 679(10) a judge may give the directions the judge thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal, the new trial, the new hearing or the hearing of the reference` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither
#ASSERT `s 679(10) a judge may give the directions the judge thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal, the new trial, the new hearing or the hearing of the reference` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application by an appellant
#ASSERT `s 679(10) a judge may give the directions the judge thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal, the new trial, the new hearing or the hearing of the reference` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a Supreme Court of Canada judge on an appellant's application
#ASSERT `s 679(10) a judge may give the directions the judge thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal, the new trial, the new hearing or the hearing of the reference` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679 the person has been released pending determination of an appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679 the person has been released pending determination of an appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the determination: no longer "pending"
#ASSERT `s 679 the person has been released pending determination of an appeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 679 the person has been released pending determination of an appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 680`

`ccc24 fixture 680a` MEANS `s 680(1) a decision made by a judge under section 522`
`ccc24 fixture 680b` MEANS `s 680(1) a decision made under subsection 524(3) to (5), (6.1) or (6.2) with respect to an accused referred to in paragraph 524(1)(a)`
`ccc24 fixture 680c` MEANS `s 680(1) a decision made by a judge of the court of appeal under section 320.25 or 679`
`ccc24 fixture 680x` MEANS `s 680(1) a decision of another kind`

#ASSERT `s 680(1) the court of appeal may review the decision and vary it or substitute another decision that in its opinion should have been made` `ccc24 fixture 680a` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 680(1) the court of appeal may review the decision and vary it or substitute another decision that in its opinion should have been made` `ccc24 fixture 680b` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 680(1) the court of appeal may review the decision and vary it or substitute another decision that in its opinion should have been made` `ccc24 fixture 680c` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 680(1) the court of appeal may review the decision and vary it or substitute another decision that in its opinion should have been made` `ccc24 fixture 680a` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no direction of the chief justice
#ASSERT `s 680(1) the court of appeal may review the decision and vary it or substitute another decision that in its opinion should have been made` `ccc24 fixture 680a` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- it confirms the decision: no vary or substitute power is engaged
#ASSERT `s 680(1) the court of appeal may review the decision and vary it or substitute another decision that in its opinion should have been made` `ccc24 fixture 680x` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 680(2) a judge of the court of appeal may exercise the powers of the court of appeal under subsection (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 680(2) a judge of the court of appeal may exercise the powers of the court of appeal under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 680(3) a decision as varied or substituted under section 680 has effect and is enforceable as though it were the decision originally made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 680(3) a decision as varied or substituted under section 680 has effect and is enforceable as though it were the decision originally made` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 682`

`ccc24 fixture 682a` MEANS `s 682(2)(a) the evidence taken at the trial`
`ccc24 fixture 682b` MEANS `s 682(2)(b) any charge to the jury and any objections that were made to a charge to the jury`
`ccc24 fixture 682c` MEANS `s 682(2)(c) the reasons for judgment`
`ccc24 fixture 682d` MEANS `s 682(2)(d) the addresses of the prosecutor and the accused`
`ccc24 fixture 682x` MEANS `s 682(2) other material`

#ASSERT `s 682(1) the judge or provincial court judge who presided at the trial must furnish the court of appeal with a report on the case` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 682(1) the judge or provincial court judge who presided at the trial must furnish the court of appeal with a report on the case` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no request
#ASSERT `s 682(1) the judge or provincial court judge who presided at the trial must furnish the court of appeal with a report on the case` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 682(2) a copy or transcript of the material shall be furnished to the court of appeal` `ccc24 fixture 682a` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 682(2) a copy or transcript of the material shall be furnished to the court of appeal` `ccc24 fixture 682a` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- dispensed with by order
#ASSERT `s 682(2) a copy or transcript of the material shall be furnished to the court of appeal` `ccc24 fixture 682b` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 682(2) a copy or transcript of the material shall be furnished to the court of appeal` `ccc24 fixture 682c` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 682(2) a copy or transcript of the material shall be furnished to the court of appeal` `ccc24 fixture 682c` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "the reasons for judgment, if any": there are none
#ASSERT `s 682(2) a copy or transcript of the material shall be furnished to the court of appeal` `ccc24 fixture 682d` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 682(2) a copy or transcript of the material shall be furnished to the court of appeal` `ccc24 fixture 682d` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no ground is based on the addresses
#ASSERT `s 682(2) a copy or transcript of the material shall be furnished to the court of appeal` `ccc24 fixture 682x` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 682(4) a party to an appeal is entitled to receive a copy or transcript of the material prepared under subsections (1) and (2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 682(4) a party to an appeal is entitled to receive a copy or transcript of the material prepared under subsections (1) and (2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "on payment"
#ASSERT `s 682(4) a party to an appeal is entitled to receive a copy or transcript of the material prepared under subsections (1) and (2)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 682(5) the Minister of Justice is entitled to receive a copy or transcript of the material prepared under subsections (1) and (2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 682(5) the Minister of Justice is entitled to receive a copy or transcript of the material prepared under subsections (1) and (2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "on request"
#ASSERT `s 682(5) the Minister of Justice is entitled to receive a copy or transcript of the material prepared under subsections (1) and (2)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 683`

`ccc24 fixture 683a` MEANS `s 683(1)(a) order the production of any writing, exhibit or other thing connected with the proceedings`
`ccc24 fixture 683b` MEANS `s 683(1)(b) order any witness who would have been a compellable witness at the trial to attend and be examined`
`ccc24 fixture 683c` MEANS `s 683(1)(c) admit, as evidence, an examination that is taken under subparagraph (b)(ii)`
`ccc24 fixture 683d` MEANS `s 683(1)(d) receive the evidence, if tendered, of any witness, including the appellant, who is a competent but not compellable witness`
`ccc24 fixture 683e` MEANS `s 683(1)(e) order that a question be referred for inquiry and report to a special commissioner`
`ccc24 fixture 683f` MEANS `s 683(1)(f) act on the report of a commissioner who is appointed under paragraph (e)`
`ccc24 fixture 683g` MEANS `s 683(1)(g) amend the indictment`

